think Opened cold: sh tools/fixtures/standing_equipment_run.sh read 41 of 41 green, guards_red=0, run_verdict=ok. Standfast clean -- REDS rows %182 through %186 all CLOSED, and the one standing row (%175, the organization-rename deep debride) is a custody gate rather than an agent-closable red.
think Lap index from git rev-list --count HEAD = 3364, so the council rota reads row 3364 mod 5 = 4 -- Earth and Mercury, the concrete. One-clock naming law, TWO_ROOMS, and the marked value. Two Rooms landed on the lap directly: a piece names its register at the top so no reader has to guess which room they stand in. That is a Status line, and the meter this lap repairs is the thing that reads Status lines.
think The previous lap's recommend named the crux: docs/CRYPTO.md at 68,547 bytes, and the first question is whether it is a door a reader enters by or a reference a reader consults, since the two want opposite repairs. Answering that meant measuring, so I ran wc -c over every tracked README.md rather than over the four the card names.
think image/README.md came back first at 400,042 bytes and lotus/README.md second at 297,878 -- both above session-logs/README.md, and neither on any roster. crypto/README.md at 88,205 and constel/README.md at 69,979 followed. Four pages past the 24,576-byte pin bound that no meter had ever read.
think The root is one file. tools/fixtures/living_docs_lint_roster.sh names which living pages living_docs_lint reads, and it was a hand-written list of 32 entries with nine module READMEs written one per for-loop. Counting the tree's own module front doors -- a tracked README.md sitting beside a tracked .rye source -- gives 34. The roster reached 6.
think Getting the discovery rule right took two passes. git ls-files 'dir/*.rye' globs across slashes, so it read active-designing/README.md and the root README as module doors on the strength of a fixture three directories down. The strict rule takes each tracked .rye path, strips its basename, and asks whether a tracked README.md sits in exactly that directory. That reads 34, and the pen proves it: an untracked README beside a tracked source passes free, which a glob would have turned into a door.
think The roster now discovers, and it drops nothing. rye/, rishi/ and aurora/ keep their sources one level down where the rule cannot see them, so they stay listed by hand -- a page dropping off a meter is a page whose pass nobody witnessed (REDS %170). It grows 32 -> 60 entries.
think Two rostered hammocks named files that had folded to active-designing/yonder/ and were never repointed. tools/d/dated_path_resolve.rish recovered both by index; the roster is repointed rather than the dated files rewritten.
obs The council rota row read this lap was Earth and Mercury -- the concrete. The marked value says every value crossing a seam wears a mark naming its type; a document crossing from writer to reader wears its Status line, and Two Rooms says name the room at the door. Widening the meter made both readable at once: duty 4 now names ten pages wanting a Status line that says which room they speak from. The row handed the lap its next round.
obs This is one lantern's third firing in five hours. A ladder table named 73 of 110 rungs (%184); a map's suffix rule reached 95 of 98 modules (%185); a meter reached 6 of 34. And tools/fixtures/index_fold_scan.sh had already written the answer into its own body four hours earlier -- discovery rather than a roster, so a room that folds tomorrow is measured the same way. The lesson reached no further than the room it was learned in, which is %186's own finding arriving on the lap after it was booked. So the rule is written into the witness where the next hand will read it.
obs The arithmetic of the blind spot, both sides on metal: against the departing roster the coverage scan reads over_bound=3; against the tree it reads over_bound=7. Four over-bound documents were invisible to the meter that exists to find them, and the ranked remainder's own table of four was measured from the roster rather than from the tree. That table is corrected in the card with all seven named.
obs over_bound ratchets rather than gates, and the honest cost is written into the scan: glow/README.md sits at 23,647 of 24,576, ninety-six percent, so ordinary growth will raise the ratchet. That is the pin law doing what it says -- fold when the pin nears its bound -- and the repair is the fold the law already names. Splitting a 400,042-byte page is a round of its own; Caravan's took a whole lap and found a red beneath it.
obs Widening the meter surfaced findings rather than faults, and the difference is worth naming. duty 2, broken relative links, reads clean over all 28 newly-measured doors -- not one break among them. duty 3's rise from 5 to 30 is definitional (a page with no inbound link from the compression shelf) rather than 25 new problems. duty 1 rose 17 -> 36 and duty 4 2 -> 11, and those are real, small, and each its own round.
obs Booking %187 carried construction/REDS.md to 24,808 bytes, past its 24,576 bound, so rows %182 and %183 folded to construction/archive/. Both folds deepened only the ../tools/ links the fold moved and left the header's ../REDS.md exactly as the destination writes it -- %186's lesson applied on the lap after it was learned, which is the whole point of writing it down.
